From c62c92f62b7a972745094f0959e815be8a5574ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:12:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir_conv: types written in bodies take omitted parameter defaults

Found while fixing 0295 (object 0.38.1): Resolve Type Aliases and Resolve Bind filled every omitted generic list
inside a body with inference variables. rustc does that only for the head of a value path (`W::new()`, `W(..)`,
`W { .. }`, patterns); a type written anywhere else in a body takes the defaults. So
- `let x: W = W(3)` with `struct W<T = u8>` was `W<i32>` (rustc `W<u8>`), and `W(3u32)` there was accepted;
- `let x: Id = Id(3)` with `struct Id<const D: bool = false>` died in typeck: "Failure to infer Infer(1) in _";
- `size_of::<Arr>()` with `type Arr<const N: usize = 3> = [u8; N]` died in Trans Enumerate: "Encountered unknown
  array size - [u8; Infer(0)]".

Both passes now mark the type of a value path (`Foo::new` / `Foo { .. }`) as the head; any other type in a body
takes the defaults when every parameter of that kind has one (a list with an undefaulted parameter is still left to
inference, lenient where rustc errors). Alias expansion monomorphises type defaults against the list filled so far
(a default naming an earlier defaulted parameter, `type C<T = u8, U = W<T>>`), and an alias's own type gets its
struct/enum/union defaults before it is copied into a body (`type B = Br;` + `B { .. }` is `Br<false>`).
object's `Builder { dynamic_symbols: Symbols::new() }` (a head, `Symbols<'data, true>` field) still infers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

